@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title VF2 subgraph-isomorphism search (Cordella et al. 2004)
[*] --> RootFrame : empty mapping
state RootFrame #D0EBFF : push root search frame\nowns_mapping = false
RootFrame --> Advance : canonical candidate pairs

state Advance #FFF3BF : inspect top frame\nadvance suspended cursor
Advance --> LimitUnwind : positive result cap is full
Advance --> Exhausted : cursor reached candidate count
Advance --> Feasibility : next candidate pair

state Feasibility #FFE8CC : kind and incident-edge checks
Feasibility --> Advance : infeasible / resume same frame
Feasibility --> Extended : feasible / push_mapping

state Extended #D3F9D8 : mapping and terminal sets extended\nundo frame recorded
Extended --> Emit : mapping covers pattern
Extended --> ChildFrame : mapping incomplete

state ChildFrame #E5DBFF : push child search frame\nowns_mapping = true
ChildFrame --> Advance : canonical child candidates

state Emit #C3FAE8 : snapshot complete embedding
Emit --> Advance : pop_mapping / resume parent

state Exhausted #FFE3E3 : pop exhausted search frame
Exhausted --> Advance : child owned mapping\npop_mapping / resume parent
Exhausted --> Done : root owned no mapping

state LimitUnwind #FFD8A8 : pop every live child frame\nand its owned mapping
LimitUnwind --> Done : caller-visible state restored

state Done #D8F5A2 : canonical result prefix\nempty mapping and stacks
Done --> [*]

note bottom of ChildFrame
  Search stack: candidate vectors and cursors are
  heap-resident continuations. Pattern depth does
  not consume native call-stack frames.
end note

note bottom of Exhausted
  Undo stack: each mapping frame restores both the
  mapping and terminal sets exactly once. It is
  separate from the search continuation stack.
end note
@enduml
